    "text": "WorldLines presents the translation of long-term memory into embodied plans as a method to address the combined challenges of partial observability and overwritten world states, not as a standalone problem definition.",
    "topic": "WorldLines framing"
  },
  {
    "text": "In the broader AI research context, translating long-term memory into embodied plans remains an open challenge, specifically when agents maintain explicit world models subject to overwriting.",
    "topic": "Broader challenge status"
  },
  {
    "text": "The necessity of translating long-term memory into embodied plans does not follow from partial observability alone; it arises only when an agent's explicit world model can be overwritten.",
    "topic": "Conditions for the challenge"
  }
